{title: Sing for Joy Forever}
{subtitle: Psalms 5:11–12}
{key: Gm}
{tempo: 85}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Gm7] | [Gm7] | [Ebmaj7] | [Gm7] |
| [Ebmaj7] | [Gm7] | [Ebmaj7] | [Am7b5] |
| [D7] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Gm7]I enter your house through a[Ebmaj7]bundant mercy
[Gm7]Bow in reverence to [Ebmaj7]your holy [Cm7]place
Lead me in [Gm7]your righteousness, O Lord
[Ebmaj7]Make your way straight before [D7]my face
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Gm7]Let all who take re[Ebmaj7]fuge in you rejoice
[Gm7]Let them sing for joy [Ebmaj7]forevermore
[Cm7]Spread your shelter o[Gm7]ver them completely
[Ebmaj7]Let those who [D7]love your name ex[Gm7]ult
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Declare them guilty, God, [Ebmaj7]in your judgment
[Gm7]Let them fall by their own [Ebmaj7]wicked schemes
[Cm7]Drive them out for [Gm7]their many transgressions
[Ebmaj7]For they have rebelled against [D7]your name
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Gm7]Let all who take re[Ebmaj7]fuge in you rejoice
[Gm7]Let them sing for joy [Ebmaj7]forevermore
[Cm7]Spread your shelter over [Gm7]them completely
[Ebmaj7]Let those who [D7]love your name ex[Gm7]ult
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Cm7]There is nothing trustwor[Gm7]thy in their mouth
[Cm7]Within them lies a path [Gm7]of destruction
[Cm7]Their throat is an o[Gm7]pen grave to all
[Ebmaj7]With their tongues they [D7]flatter in vain
{end_of_bridge}

{chorus}

{comment: Interlude}
| [Gm7] | [Gm7] | [Ebmaj7] | [Gm7] |
| [Ebmaj7] | [Cm7] | [Gm7] | [Ebmaj7] [Dm7] |
| [Gm7] | [Gm7] |

{start_of_verse: Outro}
You bless the righteous with [Ebmaj7]favor
[Cm7]Surround them with [Dm7]a shield [Gm7]of [Ebmaj7]grace
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Outro (instrumental)}
| [Gm7] | [Ebmaj7] | [Gm7] | [Gm7] |
